# Renderer & Data Contract Synchronization

## Rule
Any dashboard, modal, or display surface that renders structured data (JSONL, JSON payloads, audit logs) must have a matching renderer that:

1. Parses the structured format
2. Renders for human readability (not raw)
3. Is updated in the same commit when the data contract changes

## Examples
- Coach Command Client Briefing Recent Memory → must render as threaded conversation log (speaker labels, human timestamps, session dividers), NOT raw JSONL
- Sovereign Command Crisis Watchlist Review → same threaded format
- Sensitive Profile Activity Log → typed event renderer per event_type, not raw payload_json dump

## Forbidden
Shipping a feature that writes structured data without confirming all consumer surfaces have a working renderer for it.

## Why
Coach Command Client Briefing displayed conversations as raw `{"timestamp":"...","session_id":"...","user":"...","ai":"..."}` JSONL strings instead of readable format. Reported as fixed in Priority 2 but Flutter rendering shipped without backend renderer wiring; visual review confirmed raw JSONL still displayed.
